-        "ae4932e757e298bf82f61e1972b175f9": "**UI Construction Thought Process**\n\nAlright, let's break this down systematically. The objective is to construct a user interface for a 'main' surface using A2UI's S-Expression notation. I need a vertical list with two cards: one for dog breed information, and another for a dog breed generator. The core of this hinges on correctly interpreting the component signatures and adhering to the constraints. Specifically, I need to make sure I don't use inline definitions that conflict with the \"no explicit ID\" rules.\n\nFirst, the root will be a `Column`, with an ID of \"root\" as mandated. Rule 4 is very clear: \"Every UI component must be nested directly within a single root tree expression. Do NOT output flat adjacency lists, explicit `:id` attributes, or separate component variable IDs.\" However, to define the root as the root, I'll need to use `:id \"root\"` on the root component only.\n\nNext, I'll populate state with breed data using a `data` block. The 'Dog Breed Information' card requires a horizontal list of images. This means I'll use a `List` within the `Card` with a `:direction` of 'horizontal'. The dynamic image rendering is handled using a template with `template :item breed (Column (Image :url $/breed/url ...))`.\n\nThe 'Dog Generator' card is trickier, as it includes a `Button`, a `TextField`, and a `ChoicePicker`. Here, the signature for `Button` is key, with the `:child` parameter. The instructions say to refer to the child *by ID*, but I *must not* define explicit IDs. This presents a conundrum until I re-read the examples and re-understand the rules. After carefully going over several examples, it becomes clear that *positional* arguments (the children) are the correct way to handle this. It will simply be (Button :action (Event \"generate\") (Text :text \"Generate\")).\n\nI'll finalize the rest of the form components: text input, number input, choice picker. The generated content will be handled with a `Text` element, bound to state, and updated after generation.\n\nFinally, I'll ensure data initialization covers dog breeds, as well as the initial state variables for form input. Using `data` I will pre-populate the initial values. The state will hold the form fields and generated dog information. After that, I will construct the final S-Expression. The final structure of the UI should align perfectly with the examples, and address all requirements.\n\n\n",
-        "d040671fde187afc4d0348b43ec3cc25": "<a2ui>\n(Column :id \"root\"\n  (data\n    $/breeds [\n      (:name \"Golden Retriever\" :url \"https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/retriever-golden/n02099601_3004.jpg\")\n      (:name \"Poodle\" :url \"https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/poodle-standard/n02113799_2280.jpg\")\n      (:name \"Beagle\" :url \"https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/beagle/n02088303_12111.jpg\")\n    ]\n    $/generator/name \"\"\n    $/generator/legs \"4\"\n    $/generator/skills []\n    $/generator/generated_title \"Waiting for Creation\"\n    $/generator/generated_description \"Fill out the fields above and press Generate to create your unique fictional dog!\"\n  )\n  (Card\n    (Column\n      (Text :text \"Famous Dog Breeds\")\n      (Image :url \"https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/retriever-golden/n02099601_3004.jpg\" :description \"Dog Breed Showcase\" :variant \"header\")\n      (List :direction \"horizontal\" :children\n        (template :item breed\n          (Column\n            (Image :url $/breed/url :description $/breed/name :variant \"smallFeature\")\n            (Text :text $/breed/name)\n          )\n        )\n      )\n    )\n  )\n  (Card\n    (Column\n      (Text :text \"Fictional Dog Breed Generator\")\n      (Text :text \"Design your own custom dog breed by selecting its physical characteristics and unique powers.\")\n      (TextField :label \"Breed Name\" :value $/generator/name :placeholder \"e.g. Astro-Terrier\" :variant \"shortText\")\n      (TextField :label \"Number of Legs\" :value $/generator/legs :variant \"number\")\n      (ChoicePicker\n        :label \"Skills & Abilities\"\n        :variant \"multipleSelection\"\n        :displayStyle \"chips\"\n        :options [\"Super Speed\" \"Invisibility\" \"Laser Vision\" \"Telepathy\" \"Extreme Softness\" \"High Jump\"]\n        :value $/generator/skills\n      )\n      (Button :action (Event \"generate_breed\")\n        (Text :text \"Generate\")\n      )\n      (Divider :axis \"horizontal\")\n      (Column\n        (Text :text $/generator/generated_title)\n        (Text :text $/generator/generated_description)\n      )\n    )\n  )\n)\n</a2ui>",
