 I need to set default values for username, password, and rememberMe. My expression will be: `(data $/login/username \"\" $/login/password \"\" $/login/rememberMe false)`.\n\n3.  **Layout & Nesting:**  The structure calls for a vertical layout.  A `Column` component seems perfect for this, but the catalog states \"Children cannot be defined inline, they must be referred to by ID\". However, Rule 4 says \"Every UI component must be nested directly within a single root tree expression.\", this is a direct contradiction. I will have to pass the children inline. This means I'll be passing all the other components (Text, TextFields, CheckBox, Button) as children within the Column itself using standard nesting. It's the only way to satisfy *both* the nesting and lack of ID constraints. Thus, my root will be a `Column` element: `(Column ... (Text ...) (TextField ...)).`\n\n4.  **Addressing the Root 'root' ID:**  The spec says \"ensure there is one root component with id: 'root'\". However, I am restricted by \"Do NOT output flat adjacency lists, explicit `:id` attributes...\" This is tricky, because I can't *explicitly* set an ID.  However, this restriction only mentions \"explicit\" id attributes and that children components \"must be nested\". Also, none of the catalog signatures have `:id`, thus I can't use it even if I wanted to. Thus, the system *must* automatically recognize the first nested component as the root with ID \"root\". So, I won't explicitly add `:id \"root\"`.\n\n5.  **Button Action Implementation:**  The `Button` action needs to be linked to an event named \"login\" and pass username, password, and rememberMe status.  I have to use the `Event` action expression.  I'll form this correctly by combining the event name and the data using `:context` in an s-expression.  The correct format should be: `:action (Event \"login\" :context (:username $/login/username :password $/login/password :rememberMe $/login/rememberMe))` to ensure the correct \"event\" prope