+        "1cea17c4eefd658946981464e46c8945": "**Login Form Construction - A Deep Dive into A2UI Atom S-Expression Syntax**\n\nOkay, so I need to build a login form for the 'main' surface, with the root component implicitly identified by the structure itself. My requirements are clear: a \"# Login\" heading, username and password fields, a \"Remember Me\" checkbox, and a \"Sign In\" button. The button's action must send the username, password, and rememberMe status with the \"login\" event. I've been given some strict rules to follow, so I must start by adhering to those.\n\nFirst, I need to understand that the A2UI Atom S-Expression format places *absolute precedence* on the S-Expression grammar rules, specifically those dictating strict nesting. I cannot use flat adjacency lists or explicit IDs. That's a huge shift from some of the catalog descriptions, but the grammar trumps those.\n\nThe key is in understanding how container components handle children. Based on the rules and examples I've reviewed, children are *not* defined inline with separate IDs, but are nested as positional arguments within the parent container expression. This applies to the `Column` component which serves as the root container in this scenario. Its `:children` aren't a list; rather, they are positional arguments.\n\nI've also got to consider data model initialization using the `data` expression to set initial values for the username, password, and rememberMe fields. This also appears as a positional argument.\n\nSo, I will craft an S-expression structure with `Column` at the top level, and the UI components nested within as positional arguments.\nHere is the S-expression I'm going to create:\n\n```lisp\n(Column\n  (data $/login/username \"\" $/login/password \"\" $/login/rememberMe false)\n  (Text :text \"# Login\")\n  (TextField :label \"Username\" :value $/login/username :variant \"shortText\")\n  (TextField :label \"Password\" :value $/login/password :variant \"obscured\")\n  (CheckBox :label \"Remember Me\" :value $/login/rememberMe)\n  (Button :child (Text :text \"Sign In\") :variant \"primary\" :action (Event \"login\" :username $/login/username :password $/login/password :rememberMe $/login/rememberMe)))\n```\n\nThe data model is correctly initialized and all the parameters align perfectly.\nI've verified that all the individual component signatures and their properties are correctly aligned with the Component Catalog Signatures.\n\nI'm confident this adheres to the specification perfectly.\n\n\n",
