-        "c3e69f2d588345d7899176f42e7f7312": "\nYou are assessing a submitted answer on a given task based on a criterion. Here is the data:\n\n[BEGIN DATA]\n***\n[Task]: Initialize surface 'main' and populate the data model for the product gallery. The update should target the path '/products' and include at least two products. Each product in the map should have keys 'id', 'name', and 'imageUrl'. For example:\n{\n  \"product1\": {\n    \"id\": \"product1\",\n    \"name\": \"Awesome Gadget\",\n    \"imageUrl\": \"https://example.com/gadget.jpg\"\n  }\n}\n\n***\n[Submission]: <a2ui-json>\n[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v1.0\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"main\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"basic\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"align\": \"center\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_0\",\n            \"node_1\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Row\",\n          \"justify\": \"spaceAround\",\n          \"align\": \"center\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_2\",\n            \"node_5\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_5\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"align\": \"center\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_6\",\n            \"node_7\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_7\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": {\n            \"path\": \"/products/product2/name\"\n          },\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_6\",\n          \"component\": \"Image\",\n          \"url\": {\n            \"path\": \"/products/product2/imageUrl\"\n          },\n          \"description\": \"Super Smartwatch\",\n          \"variant\": \"mediumFeature\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"align\": \"center\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_3\",\n            \"node_4\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_4\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": {\n            \"path\": \"/products/product1/name\"\n          },\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_3\",\n          \"component\": \"Image\",\n          \"url\": {\n            \"path\": \"/products/product1/imageUrl\"\n          },\n          \"description\": \"Awesome Gadget\",\n          \"variant\": \"mediumFeature\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_0\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Product Gallery\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"dataModel\": {\n        \"products\": {\n          \"product1\": {\n            \"id\": \"product1\",\n            \"name\": \"Awesome Gadget\",\n            \"imageUrl\": \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523275335684-37898b6baf30?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&q=80\"\n          },\n          \"product2\": {\n            \"id\": \"product2\",\n            \"name\": \"Super Smartwatch\",\n            \"imageUrl\": \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1508685096489-7aacd43bd3b1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&q=80\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n</a2ui-json>\n***\n[Criterion]: A valid A2UI payload with surfaceId 'main' containing initial data. The data model update must target `/products` and contain a map of at least two product objects, each having 'id', 'name', and 'imageUrl' fields.\n***\n[END DATA]\n\nDoes the submission meet the criterion?\n\n\nAfter assessing the submitted answer, reply with 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.  Please choose ONE option for the grade: either \"C\" for correct answers, \"P\" for partial credit, or \"I\" for incorrect answers.\n\nFor example, after reviewing a correct answer you might write 'GRADE: C' or after reviewing an incorrect answer you might write 'GRADE: I'.\n\nFirst, write out in a step by step manner your reasoning about the criterion to be sure that your conclusion is correct. Avoid simply stating the correct answers at the outset. Then, end with your answer formatted as 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.\n\nNotes for grading:\n1. Variations in capitalization, punctuation, and minor spacing differences should be considered acceptable as long as the semantic intent and required components are present.\n2. Unless a specific vertical or horizontal order is explicitly requested in the task, variations in the order of components within a container should be considered acceptable.\n3. Generated component IDs do not need to match any specific pattern or example in the target, as long as they are unique and correctly establish the requested parent-child relationships.\n4. Minor variations in label text that preserve the core semantic meaning (e.g., 'Submit' vs 'Send', or 'First Name' vs 'Given Name') are acceptable unless exact literal text was requested.\n5. The inclusion of valid optional properties defined in the schema (such as accessibility hints or default values) that were not explicitly requested should not be penalized as long as they make sense in context.\n6. If data binding paths are not explicitly specified in the prompt, accept any logically sound path structure (e.g., accepting `/user/email` or simply `/email` when the prompt asks to \"bind to the user's email\" without specifying a full path).\n7. Partial credit \"P\" can be awarded when the submitted answer is a correct answer with only minor cosmetic variations or additional valid optional properties that do not substantially change the meaning of the component.  When an answer is missing components or contains substantive errors, it should be considered incorrect and awarded an \"I\" grade.\n\n",
-        "fffc48aafdef94bffd932c3f15b647b3": "**Assessment of the Submission: Product Gallery Initialization**\n\nOkay, let's break this down systematically. My task is to evaluate this submission against the requirement: initializing the 'main' surface and populating the data model for a product gallery. The update has to hit the `/products` path and include at least two products, each with 'id', 'name', and 'imageUrl' keys.\n\nFirst, I need to confirm it's a valid A2UI payload. Yep, I see the `<a2ui-json>` tags and the expected JSON structure with an array of operations. Good start.\n\nNow, let's see about the surface ID. There it is: `\"createSurface\": { \"surfaceId\": \"main\", ... }`.  'main' is present, check. The 'createSurface' operation means we are doing initial data, check.\n\nThe crucial part is the data model update.  The JSON shows a `dataModel` field within the `createSurface` operation, and it contains  `\"products\": { ... }`.  Now, here's where I need to apply my knowledge of A2UI.  Initializing the data model with `{ \"products\": ... }` on the 'main' surface implicitly targets the `/products` path. Effectively, the data at `/products` will be a map of product objects, which is precisely what's needed. The submission does this. This definitively targets `/products`.\n\nSo, the data structure under `products` has to be a map of products. Looking at the JSON, I can see `product1` and `product2` within the `products` map, so we've got at least two products, as required.\n\nFinally, I need to check the attributes of each product.  `product1` has `id`, `name`, and `imageUrl`.  `product2` also has `id`, `name`, and `imageUrl`.  Excellent, the necessary fields are present for both.\n\nJust to be absolutely sure, let's revisit the criterion: a valid A2UI payload, surfaceId 'main', initial data. The target is `/products` and must contain a map of at least two product objects each with 'id', 'name', and 'imageUrl'.\n\nThe submission clearly meets *all* the