-        "324dfbb0732e7658f9a6ed6b56c64a97": "\nYou are assessing a submitted answer on a given task based on a criterion. Here is the data:\n\n[BEGIN DATA]\n***\n[Task]: Create a UI on surface 'main' for a user settings page. Use a Tabs component with two tabs: \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\". The \"Profile\" tab should contain a simple column with a text field for the user's name. The \"# Notifications\" tab should contain a checkbox for \"Enable email notifications\". Also, include a Modal component. The modal's trigger should be a button labeled \"Delete Account\", and its content should be a column with a confirmation text and two buttons: \"Confirm Deletion\" and \"Cancel\".\n***\n[Submission]: <a2ui-json>\n[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v1.0\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"main\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"basic\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_0\",\n            \"node_1\",\n            \"node_6\",\n            \"node_7\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_7\",\n          \"component\": \"Modal\",\n          \"trigger\": \"node_8\",\n          \"content\": \"node_10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_10\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_11\",\n            \"node_12\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_12\",\n          \"component\": \"Row\",\n          \"justify\": \"end\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_13\",\n            \"node_15\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_15\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"child\": \"node_16\",\n          \"variant\": \"primary\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"confirm_delete\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_16\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Confirm Deletion\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_13\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"child\": \"node_14\",\n          \"variant\": \"borderless\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"close_modal\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_14\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Cancel\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_11\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Are you sure you want to delete your account? This action cannot be undone.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_8\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"child\": \"node_9\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"open_delete_modal\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_9\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Delete Account\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_6\",\n          \"component\": \"Divider\",\n          \"axis\": \"horizontal\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Tabs\",\n          \"tabs\": [\n            {\n              \"title\": \"Profile\",\n              \"child\": \"node_2\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"title\": \"# Notifications\",\n              \"child\": \"node_4\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_4\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_5\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_5\",\n          \"component\": \"CheckBox\",\n          \"label\": \"Enable email notifications\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/notifications/emailEnabled\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_3\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_3\",\n          \"component\": \"TextField\",\n          \"label\": \"Name\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/profile/name\"\n          },\n          \"placeholder\": \"Enter your name\",\n          \"variant\": \"shortText\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_0\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"User Settings\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"dataModel\": {\n        \"profile\": {\n          \"name\": \"Jane Doe\"\n        },\n        \"notifications\": {\n          \"emailEnabled\": true\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n</a2ui-json>\n***\n[Criterion]: The payload should target surfaceId 'main'. The main component should be a Tabs component with 'Profile' and 'Notifications' tabs. The 'Profile' tab should contain a Column with a TextField for 'name', and the 'Notifications' tab should contain a Checkbox for 'Enable email notifications'. A Modal component is also required, triggered by a 'Delete Account' button, containing a Column with confirmation text and 'Confirm Deletion' and 'Cancel' buttons.\n***\n[END DATA]\n\nDoes the submission meet the criterion?\n\n\nAfter assessing the submitted answer, reply with 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.  Please choose ONE option for the grade: either \"C\" for correct answers, \"P\" for partial credit, or \"I\" for incorrect answers.\n\nFor example, after reviewing a correct answer you might write 'GRADE: C' or after reviewing an incorrect answer you might write 'GRADE: I'.\n\nFirst, write out in a step by step manner your reasoning about the criterion to be sure that your conclusion is correct. Avoid simply stating the correct answers at the outset. Then, end with your answer formatted as 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.\n\nNotes for grading:\n1. Variations in capitalization, punctuation, and minor spacing differences should be considered acceptable as long as the semantic intent and required components are present.\n2. Unless a specific vertical or horizontal order is explicitly requested in the task, variations in the order of components within a container should be considered acceptable.\n3. Generated component IDs do not need to match any specific pattern or example in the target, as long as they are unique and correctly establish the requested parent-child relationships.\n4. Minor variations in label text that preserve the core semantic meaning (e.g., 'Submit' vs 'Send', or 'First Name' vs 'Given Name') are acceptable unless exact literal text was requested.\n5. The inclusion of valid optional properties defined in the schema (such as accessibility hints or default values) that were not explicitly requested should not be penalized as long as they make sense in context.\n6. If data binding paths are not explicitly specified in the prompt, accept any logically sound path structure (e.g., accepting `/user/email` or simply `/email` when the prompt asks to \"bind to the user's email\" without specifying a full path).\n7. Partial credit \"P\" can be awarded when the submitted answer is a correct answer with only minor cosmetic variations or additional valid optional properties that do not substantially change the meaning of the component.  When an answer is missing components or contains substantive errors, it should be considered incorrect and awarded an \"I\" grade.\n\n",
-        "03e5021c628e6a0870bf2789beebd006": "**Assessment of the JSON UI Structure**\n\nOkay, let's break this down systematically. My task is to evaluate this submitted JSON UI structure against a defined criterion for a user settings page. The core objective is to confirm if the UI meets the specified requirements.\n\nFirst, the `surfaceId` must be \"main\". Confirmed. Good start. Now, the meat of it: a \"Tabs\" component with \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\" tabs. The submission presents a Tabs component, and the titles match the prompt. The criterion clarifies that capitalization and minor punctuation variations are acceptable. \"# Notifications\" is acceptable.\n\nInside the \"Profile\" tab, we need a Column containing a text field for the user's name. The submission shows a Column and, within it, a TextField labeled \"Name\". Perfect. Moving to the \"# Notifications\" tab, it should contain a Checkbox for \"Enable email notifications.\" Again, the submission delivers, with a Column containing a Checkbox component correctly labeled.\n\nNext up, a Modal component. The submission includes a Modal. The trigger for this Modal needs to be a button labeled \"Delete Account\". Checking the trigger definition, there's a Button with the text \"Delete Account\". Excellent. Now, the Modal's content. We need a Column with confirmation text and two buttons: \"Confirm Deletion\" and \"Cancel\". The submission has a Column, and within that Column, there's confirmation text, and then a Row containing two Button components that fulfill the function. I would likely choose this organization method as well, putting the two buttons next to each other in a row is the right choice.\n\nNow, let's step back and double-check. The critical criterion focuses on the \"main component\" being a Tabs component. Wait a minute... does \"main component\" refer to the root, or is it the primary content area? The submission has a root Column which contains the Tabs, a divider, and the Modal (which is standard behavior for UI frameworks). It's common to have a root element to manage layout, especially when components like a Modal need to be triggered from elsewhere, because in many UI frameworks, the Modal itself renders the trigger. The trigger here is within the Modal definition, which is perfectly correct. My assumption that a root Column is perfectly valid is correct. This is absolutely in line with standard UI page structures. In fact, it is necessary to hold the Tabs and the Modal components (or its trigger) because they need to be on the same page.\n\nReviewing the required elements: 'main' surface, Tabs with 'Profile' and '# Notifications' (which is acceptable) tabs, the 'Profile' tab containing a Column with a TextField for 'name', the 'Notifications' tab containing a Checkbox for 'Enable email notifications', a Modal component, triggered by a 'Delete Account' button, and the Modal content a Column with confirmation text and 'Confirm Deletion' and 'Cancel' buttons. All of those elements exist in the submission, according to the criteria.\n\nThis submission meets all requirements, without question. The reasoning process confirms all the specific components, their content, and their hierarchy match exactly what the criterion specifies. The overall structure is also sound. The UI structure is perfect.\n\n\n",
-        "7050feb6175bde4125348d423810ccd2": "Based on the assessment of the submitted JSON UI configuration against the given criterion, here is the step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. **Surface Target**: The payload successfully targets the `main` surface (`\"surfaceId\": \"main\"`).\n2. **Tabs Component**: A `Tabs` component (`node_1`) is present with two tabs: \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\".\n3. **Profile Tab**: The \"Profile\" tab contains a `Column` (`node_2`) which holds a `TextField` (`node_3`) labeled \"Name\" for entering the user's name.\n4. **Notifications Tab**: The \"# Notifications\" tab contains a `Column` (`node_4`) with a `CheckBox` (`node_5`) labeled \"Enable email notifications\".\n5. **Modal Component**: A `Modal` component (`node_7`) is included. \n6. **Trigger**: The trigger is correctly set to a `Button` (`node_8`) with the text \"Delete Account\".\n7. **Modal Content**: The modal's content is a `Column` (`node_10`) containing a confirmation `Text` component (`node_11`) and a `Row` layout containing the two buttons: \"Confirm Deletion\" (`node_15`) and \"Cancel\" (`node_13`).\n\nAll requirements in the task and criteria are fully and correctly implemented.\n\nGRADE: C",
