+        "35279214c17ba66c19919bac3e9cfac9": "**UI Initialization and Data Population for Logged-In User Profile**\n\nOkay, here's the plan. We need to create a user interface for a user who has just logged in, and this involves initializing the UI on the 'main' surface, and then also populating the data model with the user's profile information. The data model needs to be set with `/user/name` to \"John Doe\" and `/user/email` to \"john.doe@example.com.\" The core of this is creating a \"root\" component (which must be named \"root\") that nests all our other elements.\n\nFirst, let's address the component hierarchy and the root component ID. The instructions and grammar are very specific: we *must* nest components directly, no explicit IDs (except the root), and no flat adjacency lists. The old style of using an `id` property to link elements is not allowed; instead, we nest the child components inside their parents directly. We must also set the `:id` of the root component. I'm going to follow the instructions and put `:id \"root\"` on the outermost component.\n\nWe'll use a `Column` as our root layout. That feels like a logical container for displaying a profile card. Now, we will initialize the data model. Rule 6 says we can use the `data` expression, so we can insert that inside the root `Column`: `(data $/user/name \"John Doe\" $/user/email \"john.doe@example.com\")`. We have to initialize the data model within the overall UI structure.\n\nI'm leaning towards a straightforward profile display, so let's start with a layout using a `Column`. I'm going to put the `data` statement at the beginning of the column, and then we'll display the user info. We will keep it simple and clean, and arrange elements to be centered vertically and horizontally. We can add an `Icon` component for an avatar, then we have the name and email as `Text` components, and add an \"Edit Profile\" button using a `Button` component that links to `edit_profile`.\n\nLet's put the whole thing together. Here's what I came up with:\n\n```lisp\n<a2ui>\n(Column :id \"root\" :align \"center\" :justify \"center\"\n  (data $/user/name \"John Doe\" $/user/email \"john.doe@example.com\")\n  (Icon :name \"accountCircle\")\n  (Text :text $/user/name :variant \"body\")\n  (Text :text $/user/email :variant \"caption\")\n  (Button :child (Text :text \"Edit Profile\") :variant \"primary\" :action (Event \"edit_profile\"))\n)\n</a2ui>\n```\n\nThat satisfies all the constraints: direct nesting, no forbidden IDs or flat lists, a root component with `id: \"root\"`, correct use of components from the catalog (with appropriate properties and variants), and initialization of the data model. And let's not forget the enclosing `<a2ui>` and `</a2ui>` tags. Good. That should do it.\n\n\n",
